        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\frac{1}{2}$",
          "worked": "Different colours is the complement of the same colour.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}P(\\text{different colours})&=1-P(\\text{same colour})\\\\P(\\text{different colours})&=1-\\frac{1}{2}\\\\P(\\text{different colours})&=\\frac{1}{2}\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
